{"name":"Tea Room","hex":"#dcb5b0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tea room","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of tearoom: a cafe or (in gay parlance only) a public lavatory."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tea_room"}],"entries":[{"title":"Teahouse","blocks":[{"text":"A teahouse or tearoom is an establishment which primarily serves tea and other light refreshments. A tea room may be a room set aside in a hotel, especially for serving afternoon tea, or may be an establishment that only serves cream tea. Although the function of a tea room may vary according to the circumstance or country, tea houses often serve as centers of social interaction, like coffee houses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Tea_room_with_interior_decoration%2C_Shantytown_Historical_Park%2C_New_Zealand.jpg/330px-Tea_room_with_interior_decoration%2C_Shantytown_Historical_Park%2C_New_Zealand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teahouse","wikidata":"Q1072166"},{"title":"Tea","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an aromatic beverage prepared by infusion of hot or boiling fresh water with fresh or cured leaves of Camellia sinensis, an evergreen shrub native to East Asia that originated in the borderlands of southwestern China, northeast India and northern Myanmar. Tea has a stimulant effect in humans primarily due to its caffeine content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg/330px-Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea","wikidata":"Q6097"},{"title":"Room","blocks":[{"text":"In a building or a ship, a room is any enclosed space within a structure, typically bounded by walls to which entry is possible only via a door or other dividing structure. The entrance connects it to either a passageway, another room, or the outdoors. The space is typically large enough for several people to move about. The size, fixtures, furnishings, and sometimes placement of the room within the building or ship support the activity to be conducted in it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Ateneul_Rom%C3%A2n_-_Sala.jpg/330px-Ateneul_Rom%C3%A2n_-_Sala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Room","wikidata":"Q180516"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Tea_house_in_Moscow.JPG/500px-Tea_house_in_Moscow.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Tea_house_in_Moscow.JPG/1280px-Tea_house_in_Moscow.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Tea_house_in_Moscow.JPG/500px-Tea_house_in_Moscow.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tea house in Moscow, 2017","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATea_house_in_Moscow.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Yu_Yuan.JPG/500px-Yu_Yuan.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Yu_Yuan.JPG/1280px-Yu_Yuan.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Yu_Yuan.JPG/500px-Yu_Yuan.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A teahouse at night in Yu Yuan Garden, Shanghai","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYu_Yuan.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Chaikhaneh_%284268013549%29.jpg/500px-Chaikhaneh_%284268013549%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki